1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:09,370
Niramoy — a voice-first pre-screening system I built. One real case, end to end.

2
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:18,180
The patient signs in with a phone number and a one-time code — no app, no account.

3
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:30,400
The assistant asks aloud and the mic opens itself — hands-free, for elderly and low-literacy patients.

4
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:42,098
The patient answers in Bangla or Banglish. Voice is primary; either way, their exact words are captured.

5
00:00:43,498 --> 00:00:52,194
The words are stored verbatim and never edited — the system's first rule. Cleaning comes later, separately.

6
00:00:53,594 --> 00:01:00,316
Behind the scenes: the AI cleans, structures, and asks follow-up questions to fill the gaps.

7
00:01:01,916 --> 00:01:07,744
Seconds later it reaches the medic — a queue ordered by urgency, not arrival time.

8
00:01:09,144 --> 00:01:16,342
The medic sees the full conversation — the patient's exact words and the follow-up questions asked.

9
00:01:17,742 --> 00:01:27,994
The AI's 10-field structured summary — which the medic verifies against the raw words.

10
00:01:29,394 --> 00:01:34,816
The medic records vitals before the case reaches the doctor.

11
00:01:36,216 --> 00:01:39,780
The medic forwards it to the doctor — who starts with safety.

12
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:55,416
Safety first: Critical, a red-flag on chest pain, and the AI's reason. The red-flag rule runs independently of the AI.

13
00:01:56,816 --> 00:02:01,518
The doctor also sees the patient's history — prior visits and prescriptions.

14
00:02:02,918 --> 00:02:10,314
The doctor accepts it into the record — a structured EHR document, an HL7 FHIR bundle.

15
00:02:11,714 --> 00:02:18,448
The prescription is the doctor's own — the diagnosis is theirs; the system never diagnoses.

16
00:02:19,848 --> 00:02:26,907
The patient speaks, the AI structures, the medic verifies, the doctor decides. Niramoy.

